"Let $P$ be a tropical polytope, let $\\overline{P}$ be a lift of $P$, and call the lift **generic** when it satisfies the genericity condition used in the source. Call $P$ **pure** when all of its maximal cells have the same dimension, and call $P$ **generic** when it satisfies the source's genericity condition.\n\n**Tropical halfspace representation conjecture.** If $P$ is pure, then the halfspaces from a generic lift $\\overline{P}$ of $P$ map to tropical halfspaces whose intersection is $P$ itself. If, in addition, $P$ is generic, then any lift works.\n\nThe preceding proposition proves the assertion under the additional hypothesis that the relevant intersection of tropical halfspaces is pure; the conjecture asserts that this purity conclusion holds in general."